01:10:51,428 --> 01:10:57,428
The French Lieutenant's Woman is a 1981 British romantic drama film directed by Karel
Reisz, produced by Leon Clore, and adapted by the playwright Harold Pinter.

13
01:16:45,714 --> 01:16:51,714
It is based on The French Lieutenant's Woman, a 1969 novel by John Fowles.

14
01:22:40,000 --> 01:22:46,000
The music score is by Carl Davis and the cinematography by Freddie Francis.

15
01:28:34,285 --> 01:28:40,285
The film stars Meryl Streep and Jeremy Irons.

16
01:34:28,571 --> 01:34:34,571
Other featured actors include Hilton McRae, Peter Vaughan, Colin Jeavons, Liz Smith, Patience
Collier, Richard Griffiths, David Warner, Alun Armstrong, Penelope Wilton, and Leo McKern.

17
01:40:22,857 --> 01:40:28,857
The film received five Oscar nominations.

18
01:46:17,142 --> 01:46:23,142
Streep was nominated for the Academy Award for Best Actress, and
Pinter for the Academy Award for Best Adapted Screenplay.

19
01:52:11,428 --> 01:52:17,428
The film explores themes of adultery, based on novel
or book, lieutenant, love, tragedy.

